# Who may sign a change to what installs BOb on a box (O-3, P5 §6.2;
# scripts/firma-instalacion.sh verificar). ONE PUBLIC KEY per line, never a
# private one:
#   henry namespaces="bob-install-chain",verify-required sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com AAAA...
# (or sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com). The principal is one plain name; the only
# options are namespaces="bob-install-chain" and verify-required, both
# required. Only a security key is accepted (Secure Enclave with Touch ID
# included); cert-authority, no-touch-required and any other option are
# refused.
# This is BOb's format, not ssh-keygen's: ssh-keygen refuses verify-required
# in an allowed_signers file ("bad options: unknown key option", OpenSSH 10.3
# and 10.6p2). verificar checks every line, gives ssh-keygen a copy of its own
# without verify-required, and itself requires both flags in the signature:
# the key was touched (0x01) and verified its user with a PIN or biometric
# (UV, 0x04). Do not hand this file to ssh-keygen directly.
# CI reads this file from main, never from the PR. A box reads its own copy,
# /opt/bob/firmantes_instalacion (root's, 644), never the checkout's. The key is
# this file's alone, not the one in firmantes_imagen.
# Empty on purpose: until Henry puts his public key here, nothing that installs
# BOb can change.
